#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# laguerre_l

#% text
# `laguerre_l(n, x)` gives the Laguerre polynomial L_n(x).

#% text
# `laguerre_l(n, a, x)` gives the generalized Laguerre polynomial L_n^a(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a non-negative integer degree the polynomial is expanded in its argument (evaluated for numbers).

#% item
# At other numeric degrees the hypergeometric representation gives the value; symbolic degrees stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
laguerre_l(3, x)
#% output
#= 1 - 3*x + (3/2)*x^2 - (1/6)*x^3

#% cell
laguerre_l(2, a, x)
#% output
#= 1 - 2*x + (1/2)*a^2 + (1/2)*x^2 + (3/2)*a - a*x

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
laguerre_l(1.5, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.5671644045780528

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `hermite_h`, `hypergeometric_1f1`
